{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1474862-how-does-instability-work-in-deviant","id":1474862,"title":"How does instability work in Deviant?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Deviant: The Renegades"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-02-17T12:37:21-08:00","id":1474862,"title":"How does instability work in Deviant?","content":"Hello, can someone explain how instability works in Deviant? I glossed over the rules and it said something that every story or chapter a Deviant gets minor instabilities equal to their highest Variation. Does that mean that a Deviant with, say, 5 dots in rapid healing, get 5 new minor instabilities every story that they have to burn off. If they do not, does it get upgraded to more severe instabilities as it &quot;rolls over&quot; in damage. I assume that over time, the deviant will finally explode due to all the mutations that they get. Is that one of the reasons that getting high level Variations is actually counterproductive to being a Deviant?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-17T20:01:41-08:00","id":1474885,"title":"","content":"That's how I understand it to work, yeah. For Deviants power <u>always</u> comes at a price","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-17T20:49:08-08:00","id":1474887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1474862-how-does-instability-work-in-deviant#post1474862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello, can someone explain how instability works in Deviant? I glossed over the rules and it said something that every story or chapter a Deviant gets minor instabilities equal to their highest Variation. Does that mean that a Deviant with, say, 5 dots in rapid healing, get 5 new minor instabilities every story that they have to burn off. If they do not, does it get upgraded to more severe instabilities as it &quot;rolls over&quot; in damage. I assume that over time, the deviant will finally explode due to all the mutations that they get. Is that one of the reasons that getting high level Variations is actually counterproductive to being a Deviant?</div> </div> </div> </div>Essentially. Deviants effectively operate on backwards advancement logic to most other splats, where the rules for buying Acclimation dots mean they can get levels of Supernatural Potency with drawbacks attached sooner than they can get purely beneficial ones, but gaining new powers or strengthening their existing ones specifically requires being in a state that precludes buying Acclimation dots.<br /> <br /> One of the benefits of being a Guardian or a Fury, of course, is that you don't pick up Instabilities through time alone, and higher Acclimation gives you a longer time before Instability has each level of effect on you, but that also makes it harder to develop new or existing Variations due to that process relying on heightened Instability.<br /> <br /> And then, of course, the main/only drawback of having higher Acclimation is that if you leave your Stability alone long enough to develop new Scars, it takes that much longer to dig your way back out, since none of the methods of healing get rid of more than one box at a time \u2014 the only real &quot;shortcuts&quot; are destroying Conviction Touchstones or leaning into your Loyalty Touchstones to heal a worse-than-minor Instability, and those come with their own risks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-18T06:39:15-08:00","id":1474896,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the clarification, so, for example. Let us assume that I create a new Deviant with a low power level, 5 dots, but I put them all in 1 variation (and 5 in a corresponding Scar to make it really fun and extreme). Can I assume that, on his first story, his Stability fills up with Minor instability, at the beginning of his second, it upgrades to medium, and by the 3rd story it has upgraded to Major so that he basically must be retired as a raving lunatic? This is just an extreme case where I go for 5 dots in variations, to get cool powers, but basically go out with a blaze of glory.<br /> <br /> This is assuming that he does nothing to mitigate his instability, but at this rate, I am guessing, he probably buys himself a story or 2 more tops before he meets his inevitable end?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-18T06:53:04-08:00","id":1474897,"title":"","content":"Or you heal the Instability before you get more of it. Characters with 5 dot Variations can be played indefinitely if you just manage to keep Instability down. It's not certain that you will manage it, but it's fully possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}